.PP
Each step returns a \f[CR]std::expected<cbor::lazy, cbor::error>\f[R].
\f[CR]and_then\f[R] passes the lazy to the next step, and the first
error reaches the end of the chain: \f[CR]key_not_found\f[R],
\f[CR]index_out_of_bounds\f[R], or \f[CR]not_indexable\f[R] when a step
meets a value that is not a map or an array.
.PP
To read one value at a known place, a path is shorter:
\f[CR]cbor::at_path<\(dq$.cars[1].hp\(dq, std::int64_t>(bytes)\f[R]
(path.md).
.PP
The next examples use \f[CR]\->\f[R] and \f[CR]*\f[R] on a
\f[CR]std::expected\f[R] with no check, so that they stay short.
A program checks each result as above, or uses \f[CR]and_then\f[R].
